e key to success in a regulated  market and gaining access to that market  is bring something useful to that market  and again  don't give away your shot if it's  offered please do get vaccinated  so as i mentioned i'm a public health  physician by training i've spent years  in and out of government and running  large global organizations i'm the chief  medical officer at danaher diagnostics  and life sciences and also run market  access and reimbursement and policy for  the company with that in mind as we move  forward through the talk today i want to  remind you of what the agenda will be  so the first part is why  it's really important to interact with  your regulator or regulating body  depending on where you are in the  country  because it allows you to move your  products forward efficiently  and  understanding  consistently what it takes to move  forward in that market  and again no matter what country you're  seeking approval in it is really  important to understand the differences  in the regulatory pathway  i'm also going to talk about how so the  basic framework for regulation of  diagnostic tests  it differs depending on what country or  region you're in i'm going to highlight  the us and the eu today but please note  that if you're in asia pac or lattam or  other areas of the world there are  always difference in differences in how  you approach your regulators and frankly  what those regulatory pathways are  and depending on where you are trying to  bring a product to market in you need to  make sure you understand those  and then the when so we need to protect  public health now as we look at what's  needed around the diagnostic space and  how to bring diagnostics to market  understanding that all of what we do  serves public health is an important  grounding piece for me it's a really  important piece again as a public health  physician to understand that at the end  of the day the products that  many of us are producing  the end user is  a patient  